    "scientific_verdict": "Exhaustive verification across F_q^n confirms three exact properties of affine coset states B + a: (1) QFT_q^{\\otimes n} |psi_{B+a}> is supported strictly on B^perp with phases omega_q^{<a, u>}, so computational-basis measurement erases the coset shift a with zero total variation distance; (2) for every off-dual classical probe u not in B^perp, the window acceptance count N_W(u; B+a) = q^{d-1} R is deterministically invariant under all shifts a in F_q^n; and (3) for every non-trivial coset shift a not in B, averaging over u in F_q^n equalizes the first-moment acceptance count to exactly q^{d-1} R regardless of whether 0 in W."
  },
  "theorems": [
    {
      "id": "T1",
      "name": "Exact QFT Dual-Subspace Support Conservation and Shift-Phase Erasure",
      "statement": "For any dimension-d subspace B in F_q^n and shift a in F_q^n, QFT_q^(tensor n) |psi_(B+a)> = q^(-(n-d)/2) sum_(u in B^perp) omega_q^(<a, u>) |u>, so computational-basis measurement after QFT_q^(tensor n) yields the uniform distribution on B^perp identically for all shifts a in F_q^n."
    },
    {
      "id": "T2",
      "name": "Deterministic Off-Dual Shift Invariance and Dual-Subspace Collapse",
      "statement": "For every probe u not in B^perp and every window W in F_q of size R, N_W(u; B + a) = q^(d-1) R = N_W(u; B) for all shifts a in F_q^n. For u in B^perp, N_W(u; B + a) = q^d * 1_(<a, u> in W)."
    },
    {
      "id": "T3",
      "name": "Exact First-Moment Equalization on Non-Trivial Cosets a not in B",
      "statement": "Averaging over uniform u in F_q^n yields E_u[N_W(u; B + a)] = 1_(0 in W) + (q^d - 1)(R/q) when a in B, whereas for every non-trivial coset shift a in F_q^n \\ B, E_u[N_W(u; B + a)] = q^(d-1) R regardless of whether 0 in W."
    }
  ],
  "title": "Planted q-ary Coset-Shift Fourier-Bias Bridge: QFT Phase Erasure, Off-Dual Shift Invariance, and Exact First-Moment Equalization on Affine Cosets B + a"
}
